Zork I source and story-image provenance
========================================

The upstream repository is a historical source collection rather than a
conventional release tarball. It contains the surviving editable ZIL source
material together with an upstream-provided Z-machine version 3 story image at
COMPILED/zork1.z3.

The story image is not generated by the Debian packaging. Git history shows
that this same upstream blob was already present in the historical source
repository in 2019 under the name COMPILED/zork1.zip; it was later renamed to
use the modern .z3 extension. In historical Infocom terminology, ZIP meant
"Z-machine Interpreter Program" and did not denote a compressed archive.

The original Infocom ZIL toolchain used to produce historical story images is
no longer available. Upstream documents ZILF, an independently maintained
modern ZIL implementation, as capable of compiling these sources with minor
issues, but also notes that the repository is a shutdown-era source snapshot
and cannot necessarily be matched exactly to a production source tree.
Consequently, rebuilding with a modern compiler is not expected to reproduce
the historical upstream story image bit-for-bit and could change game
behaviour.

For that reason this package deliberately treats COMPILED/zork1.z3 as an
upstream historical artifact and installs it unchanged. The surviving ZIL
source material remains in the Debian source package in its preferred editable
form. No compiler or generated content is downloaded during the package build,
and the build is fully offline.

The package's build-time and autopkgtest checks verify that the story image is
present, identifies itself as Z-machine version 3 data, and can be started by
Debian's Frotz interpreter. If a toolchain packaged in Debian can later be
shown to regenerate a behaviourally equivalent story image from this source
snapshot, rebuilding the installed image can be reconsidered.

Upstream snapshot handling
--------------------------

debian/watch follows the HEAD of the canonical historicalsource Git
repository and generates upstream versions in the form:

  0~gitYYYYMMDD.<short-commit>

The current package is based on upstream commit
97b7b3d68c075dd9af7da499c3e9690ada3471fd from 2025-11-20.
